@startuml
title Submit Dispute — Coordinated Idempotency, Custom Envelope
actor Customer
participant "Angular Form" as UI
participant "DisputeController" as C
participant "DisputeService" as S
database "PostgreSQL primary" as DB
Customer -> UI : Reason and description
UI -> C : POST /api/v1/disputes + JWT + Idempotency-Key
C -> S : Authenticated customer; validate + canonical fingerprint
S -> DB : Read completed record by user + operation + key
alt Existing key
  S -> S : Compare fingerprint
  S --> C : Same: replay 201 envelope; different: 409 / 2004
else New key
  group One database transaction
    S -> DB : Lock owned transaction row FOR UPDATE
    S -> DB : Re-read completed idempotency record after lock
    alt Record appeared while waiting
      S --> C : Same hash replay / different hash 409
    else Still new and eligible
      S -> DB : Verify COMPLETED, ownership, no dispute
      S -> DB : Insert OPEN version 0; UNIQUE transaction_id
      S -> DB : Insert CREATED event disputeVersion 0
      S -> DB : Insert completed 201 envelope + request hash
      S -> DB : Commit all three writes
      S --> C : 201 + Location derived from data.id
    else Missing / not eligible / already disputed
      S --> C : 404 / 1003; 422 / 2002; 409 / 2003
    end
  end
end
opt Named uniqueness collision or bounded lock timeout
  S -> DB : Roll back failed transaction
  S -> DB : Fresh transaction: read committed winner key
  S --> C : Replay / key mismatch / duplicate; timeout 503 / 3002
end
C --> UI : HTTP status + JSON envelope + Location if 201 + fresh correlation ID
UI --> Customer : Confirm / actionable error; retain unchanged retry key
note over UI, DB
No instance-local locks; shared PostgreSQL coordinates replicas.
No success before commit. At most one post-rollback lookup.
Retry-After on temporary coordination timeout; no orphan dispute/event.
end note
@enduml
